WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
The Upper Moon One Demon Kokushibo was the second&nbsp;
strongest living character in all of demon slayer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.480
just behind the demon king Muzan. And his power&nbsp;
is so incredibly overwhelming that at the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.160
the manga it took three of the strongest&nbsp;
Hashira to finally defeat him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.660
since he used to be a Demon Slayer&nbsp;
himself, I’ve always wondered what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:28.260
would have happened if Kokushibo somehow broke&nbsp;
free of Muzan’s control and became a good demon.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:34.260
And before explaining how Kokushibo would affect&nbsp;
the end of the manga, we have to ask the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:42.600
vitally important question of how would Kokushibo&nbsp;
become good? Since he is currently a demon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.000
it is normally impossible for him to betray&nbsp;
Muzan. That is because it is well known that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.140
Muzan can literally kill any demon with just&nbsp;
a single thought. But the manga has shown us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.580
that there are a few important exceptions&nbsp;
which we will discuss in just a moment.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:08.220
So I see two options for how Kokushibo could&nbsp;
become good. The first realistic option is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.840
that he never turns into a demon in the first&nbsp;
place, and fights Muzan alongside his brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.660
five hundred years ago. The second option involves&nbsp;
Tanjiro and we’ll discuss that in just a moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:27.780
but in case you forgot, in chapter 174 we learn&nbsp;
that Kokushibo is actually the brother of THE MOST&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:34.260
POWERFUL Demon Slayer in history, Yoriichi.&nbsp;
And the reason that Kokushibo became a demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.760
in the first place was because at that time&nbsp;
all of the demon slayers who had unlocked the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:45.060
Demon Slayer Mark eventually died by the time&nbsp;
they turned twenty-five. Of course, Kokushibo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:52.020
didn’t want to die, so when he encountered&nbsp;
Muzan he agreed to become a demon to survive.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.660
However, what if Kokushibo instead accepted his&nbsp;
fate, remained a human, and instead teamed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:04.740
with his brother to defeat Muzan? Now we know that&nbsp;
Yoriichi was FULLY capable of defeating Muzan on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.360
his own, so with the help of his brother, who&nbsp;
was a powerful demon slayer in his own right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.040
they should easily be able to defeat Muzan,&nbsp;
right??? Well, while that is certainly possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:19.440
we have to remember that as a human&nbsp;
Kokushibo is nowhere near the level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.300
of his brother or the demon king. So I&nbsp;
think he would be an easy target for Muzan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.220
which might lead to Yoriichi being distracted&nbsp;
and getting killed trying to save his brother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:36.060
Which is the worst possible outcome because&nbsp;
then Tanjiro would have no chance of learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.560
Sun Breathing. So while this battle honestly&nbsp;
could go either way, there is no guarantee that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.980
Kokushibo staying human and helping his brother&nbsp;
would allow them to take down the demon king.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:53.220
But with that option out of the way, let’s&nbsp;
get to the much more interesting scenario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.220 --> 00:03:00.120
where Kokushibo plays a vital role in taking down&nbsp;
Muzan at the end of the manga. In this scenario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.500
Kokushibo still becomes a demon to survive the&nbsp;
Demon Slayer Mark’s curse. And I already know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.980
that people in the comments are going to spam&nbsp;
“Haha, you idiot Ohara, don’t you know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:14.280
demons can’t betray Muzan?”. Well, yes, that is&nbsp;
normally true, but there are some exceptions. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:21.540
way Kokushibo could break free is the same way&nbsp;
this friendly doctor Tamayo did in chapter 187.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.900
While we’re not exactly sure how this happened,&nbsp;
Tamayo gained her freedom through some combination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:34.020
of her intense hatred of Muzan and the fact&nbsp;
that Muzan was nearly killed by Yoriichi. So if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.760
Kokushibo also desperately wanted to be&nbsp;
free, and Muzan had another near-death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:44.220
encounter with Yoriichi, then I think he&nbsp;
could break out of Muzan’s control too.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.580
Another option for him to gain&nbsp;
his freedom is also related to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.240
Tamayo. As we see early on in the&nbsp;
story, she turned her assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:57.540
Yushiro, into a demon all by herself. This is&nbsp;
important because Yushiro has NEVER been under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.840
Muzan’s control, which means that if the&nbsp;
human Kokushibo was looking for a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:11.340
live and somehow encountered Tamayo, then&nbsp;
she could turn him into a demon as well.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:15.660
Now both of these require some&nbsp;
luck and changes in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.980
but that’s kinda the point of a What If&nbsp;
scenario. So let’s assume that Kokushibo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:27.660
is a demon BUT he is free of Muzan’s control.&nbsp;
Now remember this is still 500 years ago and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.400
isn’t strong enough to take on Muzan himself&nbsp;
yet, so what in the world is he going to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.800
to help the current Demon Slayers? Well, he&nbsp;
could work with Tamayo or he could go into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:44.100
hiding. There’s also a very real possibility&nbsp;
that Muzan would try to hunt down Kokushibo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:51.540
but since Tamayo and Yushiro were able to hide for&nbsp;
500 years, let’s assume Kokushibo could as well.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.980
Now let’s skip ahead through the centuries.&nbsp;
Kokushibo probably wouldn’t reveal himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:02.460
unless he thought there was a serious chance&nbsp;
to defeat Muzan, which probably wouldn’t happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:08.760
until Tanjiro and Nezuko save Tamayo during the&nbsp;
Asakusa Arc. And it is possible that Kokushibo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:15.120
witnesses the event himself, or maybe Tamayo sends&nbsp;
him a message about the interesting siblings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.440
but either way, Kokushibo will be&nbsp;
keeping an eye on Tanjiro and Nezuko.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:26.460
Which is going to ABSOLUTELY change everything&nbsp;
when Tanjiro first reveals his ability to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.540
Sun Breathing during his fight against&nbsp;
the Spider Demon Rui. Which, by the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:37.140
what a legendary episode. And at this moment,&nbsp;
Kokushibo will finally feel some hope that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:43.320
new generation of demon slayers has arrived&nbsp;
to take down Muzan. So Kokushibo might reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:48.600
himself to Tanjiro now, or he might wait until&nbsp;
the young slayer unlocks the demon slayer mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:54.300
during the Entertainment District arc, but either&nbsp;
way, Kokushibo will meet with Tanjiro very soon.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:02.580
And honestly, meeting Kokushibo would be pretty&nbsp;
terrifying for anyone. Just look at his face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.920
though I suppose he could change his form&nbsp;
since he is a powerful demon. But I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.140
the best way for him to meet Tanjiro would be&nbsp;
if Tamayo invited the siblings to come visit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:18.840
That way Kokushibo could reveal himself to Tanjiro&nbsp;
while having Tamayo back up his claims that he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:24.660
actually a good demon. And knowing Tanjiro, once&nbsp;
Kokushibo has a chance to explain who he is and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:29.040
that he wants to take down Muzan, I simply&nbsp;
cannot see him refusing the demon’s help.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:37.800
However, this next part of the scenario has&nbsp;
the potential to blow up everything. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:43.620
when Kokushibo offers to train Tanjiro, I don’t&nbsp;
think the young demon slayer would want to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:48.540
this a secret from the Demon Slayer Corps.&nbsp;
Which means that Kokushibo would first need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:53.880
to come to the Demon Slayer headquarters.&nbsp;
So throw 500 years of hiding in the trash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:59.040
because it’s time for him to reveal himself&nbsp;
to the world. So let’s assume that he agrees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.360
and the leader of the Demon Slayer Corps,&nbsp;
Kagaya Ubuyashiki, allows him to come - which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:10.800
is also debatable - but this is going to lead&nbsp;
to a mind-blowing encounter with the Hashira.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:17.280
Because remember that Kokushibo chose to become&nbsp;
a demon five hundred years ago. Plus the Demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.340
slayers were nearly wiped out by Muzan during&nbsp;
this era. So there is going to be some bad blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.889
no matter what. And when you throw a certifiably&nbsp;
insane hashira like Sanemi in front of a demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.889 --> 00:07:34.440
like Kokushibo, I don’t think any words will keep&nbsp;
the wind hashira from charging in and trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:41.580
chop Kokushibo’s head off. Seriously, just look at&nbsp;
what he did to Nezuko, who was just a little girl.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:46.860
Now I don’t think there is any chance Sanemi&nbsp;
succeeds, although it is fair to say that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:53.280
version of Kokushibo probably isn’t as powerful&nbsp;
if he stopped eating humans. Regardless he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.260
still be an incredibly strong demon who&nbsp;
has been training for five hundred years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:03.840
and it would likely take multiple Hashira to&nbsp;
take him down. However, I don’t think Kagaya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:10.980
would let that happen since he invited him,&nbsp;
so after a few sword clashes he orders the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:16.560
fighting to stop and for you to subscribe to&nbsp;
the channel for more anime content like this.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:24.180
But now Kokushibo can finally explain who he&nbsp;
is and that he wants to take down Muzan. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.920
not JUST as a fighter, but honestly he would&nbsp;
probably make a much bigger difference as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:34.560
teacher because he could show them many of&nbsp;
the secrets of the old Demon Slayer Corps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:39.180
This includes some abilities that they already&nbsp;
know such as Total Concentration Breathing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:44.760
but also others such as being able to see the&nbsp;
Transparent World and even more information about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:52.620
the Demon Slayer Mark. And man, this is going to&nbsp;
DRAMATICALLY change the final clash against Muzan.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:58.740
However, I still don’t think many of the&nbsp;
Hashira would want to train with a demon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:06.300
but I’m sure Tanjiro would accept with Kagaya’s&nbsp;
approval, especially because Kokushibo could show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:13.380
him more about Sun Breathing since his brother&nbsp;
invented it 500 years ago. Zenitsu and Inosuke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.220
would probably also join in the training,&nbsp;
and even though they might not be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.840
unlock access to the transparent world or the&nbsp;
full demon slayer mark just by practicing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:28.620
I am 100 percent sure that training with&nbsp;
a super strong 500 year old demon would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:32.940
give all three of them an incredible&nbsp;
power boost going into the next arc.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:38.820
And with a greater mastery of Sun Breathing&nbsp;
and Total Concentration breathing, Tanjiro is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:45.540
absolutely going to crush the demons during the&nbsp;
Swordsmith Village arc. In fact, Tanjiro’s new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:51.840
powers might let him take out the Upper Moon 4&nbsp;
Hantengu’s true body and his emotion-based forms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:57.060
before they can even combine into their strongest&nbsp;
form. And when the Love Hashira Mitsuri and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:02.460
Mist Hashira Murichiro see just how powerful&nbsp;
Tanjiro has become since training with Kokushibo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:09.840
I think this will finally convince the other&nbsp;
Hashira to learn from Kokushibo. Who knows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:16.620
maybe Tanjiro would even be strong enough to&nbsp;
officially become a Hashira at this point.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:22.740
Which is honestly just the start of how much this&nbsp;
good version of Kokushibo will change the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:27.540
but from this point let’s assume that Muzan still&nbsp;
finds out about Nezuko’s resistance to the sun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:33.660
so the plot progresses mostly unchanged.&nbsp;
This leads to another intense training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:37.260
arc before the Demon Slayer Corps&nbsp;
are then attacked by the Muzan.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:42.540
Alongside the demon king are the remaining Upper&nbsp;
Moon demons, including a brand new demon, since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:49.200
Kokushibo is not on their side. As for who would&nbsp;
be the new Upper Moon One, it could honestly go a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:54.780
few different ways. The easiest thing would be for&nbsp;
the old Upper Moon 2 Doma to simply be promoted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.780 --> 00:11:00.960
with Akaza moving up behind him to number two. Or&nbsp;
the other option is that Muzan convinced another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:11.040
strong demon slayer to join his side and this&nbsp;
new demon became Upper Moon one. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:17.400
Kokushibo’s presence during the final battle&nbsp;
is going to change things in SO MANY WAYS.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:22.620
The start of this battle will go as usual, since&nbsp;
Muzan was able to catch the Demon Slayers by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:28.320
surprise in the original story. This means that&nbsp;
Kagaya still talks with Muzan and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:33.960
blows himself up. Then Tamayo poisons Muzan. At&nbsp;
this point, the Demon Slayers arrive along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:41.580
Kokushibo, and this is where things start to go&nbsp;
absolutely crazy. Muzan is furious that multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:47.700
demons are siding with the Demon Slayers, and he&nbsp;
is especially pissed off when he recognizes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:55.020
Kokushibo is Yoriichi’s brother. So he’d probably&nbsp;
go berserk and try to kill them all instantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.580
but since everyone here is now stronger&nbsp;
because of their training with Kokushibo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:05.640
they can defend against the attack without&nbsp;
anyone getting hurt. Then Kokushibo might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:11.040
able to occupy Muzan long enough for the&nbsp;
other demon slayers to deal significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:17.280
damage. But in the end, I think this version of&nbsp;
Kokushibo is weaker than in the original story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.600
so they probably wouldn’t be&nbsp;
able to defeat Muzan right here.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:27.180
But that’s just the start of the battle because&nbsp;
then Muzan drops them into the Infinity Castle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:32.340
so that he can recover from Tamayo’s poison. This&nbsp;
splits up the Demon Slayers to fight against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:39.120
Upper Moon Demons. And here is where we have some&nbsp;
interesting choices. Because originally Tanjiro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:40.668
and the water hashira Giyu fought against Akaza;&nbsp;
the insect hashira Shinobu, her apprentice Kanao,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.668 --> 00:12:50.280
and Inosuke fought against Doma; and Muichiro,&nbsp;
Genya, Sanemi, and the Stone Hashira Gyomei fought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:55.620
against Kokushibo. But since Kokushibo is on&nbsp;
the Demon Slayer Corps side now, one of two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:00.960
things could occur. First Kokushibo could fight&nbsp;
against whatever new demon is the Upper Moon 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.580
And this is a bit tricky since normally demons&nbsp;
can’t kill each other with sunlight, but let’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:12.060
assume that Kokushibo can use a Nichirin blade&nbsp;
and can kill demons. That would free up Muichiro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:17.940
Genya, Sanemi, and Gyomei to help the others.&nbsp;
Or the other option is those four could still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:22.200
fight whatever new demon is the upper&nbsp;
moon one, while Kokushibo helps fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:26.580
some of the other strong demons. Whatever&nbsp;
the case, there are more strong fighters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:32.520
to help with the battles, so we could even&nbsp;
see Shinobu and Muichiro survive this time.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:37.140
Now by the time, Yushiro forces everyone out of&nbsp;
the Infinity Castle, I think there is a strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:43.260
chance that almost all of the Hashira are still&nbsp;
alive. Maybe only Genya dies, but overall the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:48.480
Demon Slayers are in a much stronger position&nbsp;
to fight Muzan for Round Two. And thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:53.220
Kokushibo’s training, I think most of them&nbsp;
would be able to see the transparent world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:59.040
which would greatly help them defend against&nbsp;
Muzan’s unbelievably fast tentacle attacks.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:04.980
Which leads us to the epic final clash, which&nbsp;
honestly is still going to be unbelievably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.760
difficult. At this point, there is still an&nbsp;
hour and a half until dawn. And honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:14.220
Muzan may simply realize that this situation is&nbsp;
dangerous for him and he might try to run away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:18.540
immediately. However, for the sake of the story&nbsp;
let’s assume that he decides to stay or that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:23.940
they can somehow stop him from leaving. That means&nbsp;
they either need to delay Muzan until sunrise or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:29.640
cut through all twelve of his vital organs. Which&nbsp;
interestingly there are exactly twelve fighters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:34.620
facing off against Muzan if we include all the&nbsp;
surviving demon slayers and Kokushibo. So I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:41.940
just imagine an unbelievably epic final scene with&nbsp;
each one of them destroying one of Muzan’s organs.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:46.860
And that could even let us avoid the whole&nbsp;
Tanjiro turning into a demon mess - I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:52.020
that was always kinda weird in the first place&nbsp;
-which means that because Kokushibo became good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:56.100
many more of the Hashira were able to&nbsp;
survive the final battle. But I wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.100 --> 00:15:00.120
if everyone could have lived if another&nbsp;
strong demon were to join their side.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:04.080
I’m actually talking about Demon Rengoku,&nbsp;
and if you want to know what would happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:09.540
if Rengoku accepted the offer to become a&nbsp;
demon, you can watch that video right here.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:13.020
Thanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

